{"severity":"warning","file":"errors/copy_shared_6.march","start_line":9,"start_col":29,"end_line":9,"end_col":31,"message":"`List.map` builds a new copy instead of reusing `xs` in place, because `xs` is used again afterwards.\nA function can update a value in place only when it holds the only reference to it; `List.append` also holds `xs` until it runs, after `List.map`.","code":"copy_shared","fix":null,"labels":[{"file":"errors/copy_shared_6.march","start_line":9,"start_col":16,"end_line":9,"end_col":18,"message":"`xs` is also passed to `List.append` here, which runs after `List.map`"}],"notes":[],"category":"COPY"}
